Lore: {
	LoreSilva: {
		DisplayName: Silva, the Goddess of Life
		Tooltip: ""
		Lore:
			'''
			The goddess of life and the elemental of nature. She wears many titles.
			Silva is the only other god besides Xeroc to have perfectly ascended. Holding the power of the world's life itself.
			Due to her being a god, she was against my movement the moment it started. 
			She approached me with her champion, Braelor and tried to reason with me to stop my crusades.
			Her compassion towards me and the coming of the crusades did persuaded me, though I did not let her words fully convince me.
			In return, I rose and challenged her. While Braelor was able to make out with his life, Silva wasn't so lucky.
			Although, due to her being an elemental and the goddess of life, she wasn't able to die. Not without the destruction of her domain.
			By the end, she was motionless, but still alive. With that, I picked her up and tossed her into the abyss for her second time.
			Since then, she remained deep in the depths of the abyss. Healing in her cocoon until you forcibly freeded and bested her.
			What you fought was only a fraction of her full power. 
			And it will take a long while for her to return at her full power again. Long past both our times.
			'''
	}

	LorePrimordialWyrm: {
		DisplayName: Primordial Wyrm
		Tooltip: ""
		Lore:
			'''
			The wyrm was the first of its kind, the first to graze the abyss. 
			Despite this, its size and age isn't what makes it so powerful.
			After I had thrown Silva's body into the abyss, the wyrm came to aid her and her cocoon's construction.
			Due to this amount of generosity, Silva's powers seeped out and came to bless the wyrm to thank it for all it had done.
			After this blessing, the wyrm was given a permanent task. The task to guard the Terminus.
			This task then gave it markings of primordial light along its body, as a symbol of its power and what to protect.
			Although, not too long after, the wyrm would come to hate this symbol, and the energy it leaked out in the darkest waters.
			It would start to attack anything that would illuminate the depths. With the power granted slowing driving it insane.
			It sent the deep abyss into a period of darkness, a period void of sight. Everything that used to light the abyss, now destroyed.
			All that illuminates the depths now are the twinkles of lumenyl within the walls of the deep abyss. Walls it cannot destroy.
			I do give my deepest sympathy to the wyrm.
			It did not ask for this power, and it did not ask for the insanity that it would come with. 
			Yet another hallmark of what the Gods have done.
			'''
	}

	LoreTerminus: {
		DisplayName: The Terminus
		Tooltip: ""
		Lore:
			'''
			During the Dragonic Era, the leader of the dragon monks carved out a large stone from the Aerie.
			The monk would use it for various rituals, soon carving the sigil of Primordial Light into the face of said stone.
			Though, as the dragons fought off Fovos, The Moon Lord, the monk would approach Zeratros for a final time.
			In a ritual with the stone, the monk would kill Zeratros, becoming Xeroc. This stone would be called "The Terminus".
			After Zeratros' death, and soon after Xeroc witnessed providence's imperfect ascension, Silva would approach Xeroc.
			She was someone already well respected by the monks, and would come to ask Xeroc for the Terminus to ascend.
			Using the Terminus, Xeroc would help Silva ritualistically take the soul from the dragon of life.
			As Silva perfectly ascended, Xeroc finally noticed something about Silva's ascension compared to Providence's attempt.
			The Terminus was the key to prefect ascension. Without it, all ascensions would be impure.
			As a final act of selfishness, Xeroc and Silva would bless the Terminus before then locking it away deep in the abyss.
			Others would come to ask for the Terminus for themselves, though Xeroc nor Silva would reveal its location.
			Even I did not know where it was kept until now. Though still, I doubt its useful for the purpose it once served.
			'''
	}
}
